What makes you think his earnings are from capital gains? He doesn't really sell many properties from what I am aware and we don't know if he's much of an investor in the markets. Something tells me he's not. The majority of his money seems to come from shady real estate deals with Russians and leasing his name to buildings, some clothing products, etc.   


I don't think it's even so much about what he files or his tax rate. It's that you can compare what people report on taxes to other sources to determine fraud. According to Cohen he fudges the valuations of properties, etc. for insurance purposes, I imagine he fudges a lot of information on his returns as well. Or, conversely, maybe they're pristine, and having them will just help illuminate the other things he lies about. Like his actual worth, which at the end of the day is probably what he's most concerned about. 

&amp;#x200B;
